  "id": "Compound::DB01078 - Gene::476",
  "verbalization": "Deslanoside appears to interact with Atp1a1 through a shared pathway involving Fxyd2 and potassium-transporting ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Deslanoside binds to Fxyd2, which is involved in potassium transport, and this interaction leads to the participation of Fxyd2 in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, which in turn is associated with Atp1a1. This indicates a potential mechanism where Deslanoside influences Atp1a1 through a regulatory role in potassium transport. The connection is further supported by the presence of a similar pathway involving Atp1b2, which also participates in sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activity and is linked to Atp1a1. The overlapping roles of Fxyd2 in both potassium-transporting and sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activities suggest a possible functional overlap, which may explain the shared interaction with Atp1a1. The evidence highlights a mechanism where Deslanoside modulates Atp1a1 through a pathway involving Fxyd2, emphasizing the role of potassium transport in the drug's effect on Atp1a1.",
